<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21352" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Idmon</span></b> , ŏnis, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴδμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The father of Arachne</i>, <i>a native
				of Colophon</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Idmŏnĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>related to Idmon</i>, <i>Idmonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arachne,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 133</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A prophet in Argos</i>, <i>the son of
				Apollo and Cyrene</i>, <i>one of the
			Argonauts</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib. 506</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				14</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Rutulian</i>, <i>messenger of
				Rutulus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 12,
			75</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>The physician of Adrastus</i>, <i>of
				Epidaurus</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 3, 398</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
